Take the textures of Lemma \claimref{neutrino.breaking-relation} at the $S_{3} 	o S_{2}$ direction $E = e_{3}e_{3}^{\mathsf{T}}$, as in Proposition \claimref{synthesis.theta23-at-s3-s2-direction}: in each sector a matrix $M(X) = \J + \delta(E + X)$ (times the sector's scale), with $\delta$ real and $X$ real and odd under the exchange $P_{12}$ of the first two families (the $S_{2} 	o 1$ stage of Proposition \claimref{synthesis.solar-angle-light-plane-sum-rule}), the charged leptons reading $M_{e} = M(X_{e})$ with $\delta = \delta_{c}$ and the neutrinos $m_{
u} = \mD M_{R}^{-1}\mD^{\mathsf{T}}$ with $\mD = M(X_{
u})$ and $M_{R} = \alpha\Pi + M_{3}\J/3$, $\alpha, M_{3} 
eq 0$. Call $XP_{12}$ the \emph{twin} of $X$.
 egin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] The twin map is a linear involution of the $P_{12}$-odd matrices that exchanges the symmetric ones with the antisymmetric ones: with $X_{s}(s,b) =  igl[ egin{smallmatrix} s & 0 & b \ 0 & -s & -b \ b & -b & 0 \end{smallmatrix} igr]$ and $X_{a}(c,e) =  igl[ egin{smallmatrix} 0 & c & e \ -c & 0 & -e \ -e & e & 0 \end{smallmatrix} igr]$, $X_{s}(s,b)P_{12} = X_{a}(s,b)$ and $X_{a}(c,e)P_{12} = X_{s}(c,e)$. In the basis of the odd line $(1,-1,0)$ and the even plane it keeps the (odd, even) entries $x$ of $X$ and reverses the (even, odd) entries $y$.
