\emph{(i) The odd part.} The exchange $P_{12}$ fixes $u'$ and $e_{3}$, so $P_{12}\mathbb{1}P_{12} = \mathbb{1}$, $P_{12}\J P_{12} = \J$, $P_{12}EP_{12} = E$ (Lemma \claimref{neutrino.breaking-relation} for $\J$, $\Pi = \mathbb{1} - \J/3$ and $E$), and $u'\wedge s$ is $P_{12}$-invariant by Proposition \claimref{synthesis.residual-s2-fixes-120-family-form}(i). The shift $S$, $Se_{j} = e_{j+1}$ (indices mod $3$), has $S + S^{\mathsf T} = \J - \mathbb{1}$, even, and $S - S^{\mathsf T} = A$ with $Av = v\cdot(I_{e}u')$, $I_{e} = e_{1}e_{2}e_{3}$ the unit pseudoscalar of family space: the contraction of $v$ with the bivector dual to $u'$. A permutation matrix $P$ is orthogonal, so it extends to an automorphism of the algebra of family space sending $I_{e}$ to $\det P\,I_{e}$, and $P(v\cdot(I_{e}u')) = (Pv)\cdot(\det P\,I_{e}Pu') = \mathrm{sgn}(P)\,(Pv)\cdot(I_{e}u')$, so $PAP^{\mathsf T} = \mathrm{sgn}(P)A$: $A$ spans a copy of the sign representation, odd under every transposition and fixed by the $3$-cycles. The odd part $X \mapsto 	frac12(X - P_{12}XP_{12})$ is linear; it kills the five even structures and sends $S$ and $S^{\mathsf T}$ to $\pm	frac12 A$, so the odd part of the complex span is $\C A$, and without $S$ and $S^{\mathsf T}$ (which enter only through the circulant reading of (ii)) it is zero. The sign representation occurs once in $M_{3}$: by characters, $M_{3} = V\otimes V$ with $V = \mathbf{1}\oplus\mathbf{2}$ the permutation representation, and $V\otimes V = 2\cdot\mathbf{1}\oplus\mathbf{sgn}\oplus 3\cdot\mathbf{2}$, since $\mathbf{2}\otimes\mathbf{2} = \mathbf{1}\oplus\mathbf{sgn}\oplus\mathbf{2}$; the check computes the space $\{X : PXP^{\mathsf T} = \mathrm{sgn}(P)X\  orall P\}$ as an exact kernel and finds dimension one. It is antisymmetric (the symmetric matrices, $\mathrm{Sym}^{2}V = 2\cdot\mathbf{1}\oplus 2\cdot\mathbf{2}$, contain no sign representation).

